  "notes": "Semi-phosphorylative Entner-Doudoroff pathway (M00308): gluconate => glycerate-3P. Starts with unphosphorylated gluconate, then phosphorylates KDG to KDPG before cleavage. Found in archaea and some thermophilic bacteria. Diagnostic feature: kdgK (2-dehydro-3-deoxygluconokinase) phosphorylates KDG to KDPG, then eda cleaves KDPG. Produces G3P which is further oxidized to glycerate-3P. Hybrid pathway - starts non-phosphorylated, becomes phosphorylated mid-pathway.",
